WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:02.969
[indistinct chatter]

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.777
[sighs]

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:11.944
Here is your white wine.

00:00:11.977 --> 00:00:13.513
- Thank you.
- You are welcome.

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:14.647
Hey, Pete.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.382
Little--
little thirsty tonight?

00:00:16.415 --> 00:00:18.117
Ha, yeah.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:19.252
Super thirsty.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.253
[laughs]

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:21.487
Pete,
this is Haraysa.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:22.789
Haraysa, this is Pete.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.891
Haraysa just got back
from Africa.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.694
Oh, Africa.

00:00:30.896 --> 00:00:32.432
Anyways, uh, where was I?

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:33.866
Oh, the AUC.

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:35.535
Oh, right,
so this conflict

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:38.137
is exactly the reason
the African Union Commission

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:39.472
was put in place
to address.

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:41.140
(Haraysa)
The organization
of African Unity

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:42.375
certainly wasn't
gonna do anything.

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:43.509
Oh, exactly.

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:45.445
And if Nkosazana Dlamini-Zuma

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.113
wants to do anything
about Bangui,

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:48.448
she's certainly
being quiet about it.

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.882
The worst part about Bangui

00:00:49.915 --> 00:00:51.717
is that no one knows
what's going on.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:52.718
Oh, no, I know.

00:00:52.751 --> 00:00:53.753
I mean,
look at right next door,

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:54.854
the South Sudan.

00:00:54.887 --> 00:00:55.888
Here's the thing.

00:00:55.921 --> 00:00:57.090
Everybody just thinks
that it's like--

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.224
that it's the damn
<i> Lion King</i> over there.

00:00:58.257 --> 00:00:59.225
You know?

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:00.393
<i> Lion King.</i>

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:04.531
Excuse me?

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.868
It's not
<i> The Lion King.</i>

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:12.538
Exactly.

00:01:12.571 --> 00:01:13.806
I mean,
what do people think?

00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:15.141
A...

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:18.144
baboon is going
to hold a lion cub

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:20.780
over a rock,
up to the sun,

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:23.483
while all
the little animals sing?

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:27.887
Anyway...

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:28.888
Um...

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:29.922
So I also wanted
to mention is,

00:01:29.955 --> 00:01:31.357
they have the manpower,

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:33.593
because AMISOM
has 25,000 troops

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.261
just sitting there
in Somalia.

00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:39.899
It's not a "three
animated hyenas" situation.

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:41.834
That doesn't make
any sense.

00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:45.805
The bad guy isn't Scar
over there.

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:47.240
Um...yeah.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.274
Yeah, that's right.

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:50.576
It's not like
Scar's the bad guy.

00:01:50.609 --> 00:01:52.545
Well, I mean, you know,
the truth is,

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:54.480
no one knows who to blame,

00:01:54.513 --> 00:01:55.681
because in reality,

00:01:55.714 --> 00:01:58.084
AMISOM doesn't have
that much control.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.086
- They don't.
- Like Simba.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:01.854
Oh, like Simba.

00:02:01.887 --> 00:02:04.357
He had no control over--

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.460
Well, he was plucked out
from his home

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:09.695
and went on a whole journey

00:02:09.728 --> 00:02:10.830
before he came back

00:02:10.863 --> 00:02:12.965
and was just
in the middle of a war.

00:02:12.998 --> 00:02:14.901
Really had nothing
to do with him.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.003
You know, Pete,
I'd be really interested

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.104
in hearing your thoughts

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:20.140
on the UN's policies
in East Africa.

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:23.910
<i> Hakuna matata.</i>

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:24.911
[scoffs]

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.979
Unbelievable.

00:02:27.012 --> 00:02:28.915
Yes.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:32.618
My God,
that sums it up perfectly.

00:02:32.651 --> 00:02:34.954
There's so much work
still to be done.

00:02:34.987 --> 00:02:36.389
Yes, that's what
I was saying.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.291
This has been going on
for so many years.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.159
So many years,
<i> Circle of Life.</i>

00:02:40.192 --> 00:02:41.761
Hmm.

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:44.096
Exactly,
that's really brilliant.

00:02:44.129 --> 00:02:45.298
I'm not brilliant.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.300
Let's dial it back.

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.401
I'm just a man.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.436
Okay, uh, I'm gonna--

00:02:50.469 --> 00:02:53.606
I'm gonna go get
some hors d'oeuvres.

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:55.542
Okay, no need
to announce it.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:03.482
What are your thoughts
on the Middle East?

00:03:03.515 --> 00:03:04.551
<i> Aladdin.</i>

00:03:06.952 --> 00:03:08.188
Huh.

